  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat is the price of a movie ticket on the last Friday? Colby's parents give him $155 each month to spend at the movies.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The information given is not sufficient to determine the ticket price. Knowing that Colby has **$155 per month** does not tell us:\n\n- how many Fridays are in the month,\n- whether he goes to the movies every Friday, or\n- whether he spends all $155 on tickets.\n\nTherefore, the price of a ticket on the last Friday **cannot be determined** from the given information.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Cannot be determined}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Colby's parents give him $150 each month to spend at the movies.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Changing the allowance to **$150 per month** still does not provide enough information to determine the price of a movie ticket on the last Friday.\n\nWe would need to know how many movie tickets Colby buys or how his monthly money is divided. Thus,\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Cannot be determined}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Oh, I forgot to mention: Tickets for movies on Fridays and Saturdays cost $11, while tickets on all other days cost $7.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Tickets on **Fridays and Saturdays** cost \\$11. Since the last Friday is a Friday, the movie ticket costs\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$11}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Tickets for movies on Fridays and Saturdays cost $10, while tickets on all other days cost $7.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The last Friday is a **Friday**, and Friday tickets cost **\\$10**.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$10}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: the last Friday is a regular Friday, not a holiday or special event.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Since the last Friday is a regular Friday, the Friday ticket price applies:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$10}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Here's another detail: Colby buys his ticket at the standard box-office price.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "A regular Friday ticket at the standard box-office price costs **$10**. The monthly allowance does not affect the ticket’s price.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$10}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Thanks, that helps. Now I want to figure out: How many additional movies can Colby see on the last Friday while staying within his monthly movie budget? By the way, here are some relevant details: A tub of popcorn costs $8, and a box of candy costs $2. Colby has already seen 5 movies on Fridays or Saturdays and 8 movies on other days during the month. Colby has already had 2 tubs of popcorn and 4 boxes of candy during the month, and he wants one tub of popcorn and one box of candy on the last Friday.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Colby’s monthly budget is \\$150.\n\n**Cost of movies already seen:**\n\n\\[\n5(\\$10)+8(\\$7)=\\$50+\\$56=\\$106\n\\]\n\n**Cost of snacks already purchased:**\n\n\\[\n2(\\$8)+4(\\$2)=\\$16+\\$8=\\$24\n\\]\n\n**Cost of snacks on the last Friday:**\n\n\\[\n\\$8+\\$2=\\$10\n\\]\n\nTotal spent including the planned snacks:\n\n\\[\n\\$106+\\$24+\\$10=\\$140\n\\]\n\nMoney remaining:\n\n\\[\n\\$150-\\$140=\\$10\n\\]\n\nSince a movie on Friday costs \\$10, Colby can see\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]\n\nadditional movie on the last Friday.",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
